Parity reproduced exactly from the web source (cross-platform value parity, NOT a "corrected"
version): savings banner shown iff potential_monthly_savings > 5, title interpolates
fmtNumber(savings,0); battery score = RadialGauge(value/100) tiered #22c55e/#f59e0b/#ef4444 →
statusSuccess/Warning/Danger; peak-session % red iff > 30; peak/off-peak hours = map(h => `${h}:00`)
.join(', ') || '—'; heatmap maxCost = peakCostPerKwh || 0.30, intensity = min(1, cost/maxCost),
cell rgba(round(i*239), round((1-i)*187), round((1-i)*100), min(0.9, 0.15 + sessions*0.12)), empty =
rgba(255,255,255,0.02), legend stops [0.15,0.3,0.5,0.7,0.9]; recommendation savings chip iff
estimated_savings != null && > 0; fmtNumber = en_US grouped fixed-fraction half-up; formatCurrency =
"$" + fmtNumber. The surface uses no Recharts/Leaflet (web "Charts/maps used: none") — gauge is a
Shape arc, heatmap is rectangles; no Swift Charts import.

